  "question": {
    "text": "A force $\\mathrm{F}=\\alpha+\\beta \\mathrm{x}^2$ acts on an object in the x -direction. The work done by the force is 5 J when the object is displaced by 1 m . If the constant $\\alpha=1 \\mathrm{~N}$ then $\\beta$ will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uAnOt",
      "text": "$15 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MYQ0t",
      "text": "$12 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "6kFTu",
      "text": "$8 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cSasS",
      "text": "$10 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$F=\\alpha+\\beta x^2$\nWork done $\\int d w=\\int F \\cdot d x$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Delta W=\\int F \\cdot d x=\\int\\left(\\alpha+\\beta x^2\\right) d x \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Delta W=\\left|\\alpha x+\\frac{\\beta x^3}{3}\\right|_0^1=\\alpha+\\frac{\\beta}{3}=5\n\\end{aligned}$\nGiven $\\alpha=1$\nSo, $\\frac{\\beta}{3}=4$\n$\\Rightarrow \\beta=12 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$",
    "image": null
  },
